  <title>CS 336: Language Modeling from Scratch</title>
  <dc:creator>Rohan Rajput</dc:creator>
  <link>https://rohanrajput04.github.io/courses/cs336-language-modeling-from-scratch/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<p>Stanford <a href="https://cs336.stanford.edu/">CS 336 — Language Modeling from Scratch</a>, Spring 2026. Instructors: Tatsunori Hashimoto and Percy Liang.</p>
<p>The course walks through building a modern language model end-to-end: tokenization, architecture, optimization, parallel training, inference, scaling laws, data curation, and post-training alignment (SFT, RLHF, DPO, RL for reasoning).</p>
<p>My notes for each lecture and assignment live on the pages below. They’re placeholders until I’ve actually worked through the material.</p>
